# Image Classification Using R and Deep Learning

## Project Overview

This project implements a basic image classification system using **R Programming** and a neural network. The project reads JPEG images, preprocesses them by resizing and converting them into numerical feature vectors, trains a deep learning model, and predicts the classes of unseen test images.

The implementation demonstrates an end-to-end machine learning workflow in R, including image processing, data preparation, model building, training, evaluation, and prediction.

## Project Objective

The objective of this project is to develop a simple image classification model using R and deep learning techniques.

The model is trained using images from two different classes and then used to predict the class of new test images.

## Dataset Information

The dataset consists of 12 JPEG image files divided into two categories:

### Class 0

- p1.jpg
- p2.jpg
